#-    §5✐ Authors Note ✐
§d****************************§

§8So... here we all are yet again! Ready to say goodbye once more and another hello on the 'other side'. This season has been so much fun and I'll miss it. Deathcap keeps growing and I don't think it will ever stop ;) See you soon...§r
§7§sStarSweetpea x
#- §5Any more thoughts...§r
§6About what? We left it all too late! How can we expect to find §cCastien§6, learn how to survive §0The Darkness§6, and regain all my old memories before we all reset in a flash!?
§5I'm not sure my dear, but one thing I am sure off...        is us! 
I have faith in us. 
We can find a way.§r
#- §6The lantern's are too powerful for us, the strange 'christmas gift' anomaly was 
a 'once in a year' opportunity that I messed up... §r😢
§5Don't be so hard on yourself, I hate seeing you like this.§

§6I'm a failure, stumbling through all the chaos while the world inches closer to ending.§r..
#-  §5╔══--ஓ๑☠๑ஓ--══╗§r
       §8No Control§r
 §5╚══--ஓ๑☠๑ஓ--══╝§r
§dSweetpea sat cross-legged on the floor of her main Deathcap Office, her head in her hands, while §5ɨȶ§r hovered near §dthe edge of the room, people-watching out the huge window overlooking 
Deathcap Island.§r§r
#- §6"I failed you, 
myself... all my friends... Craftadia..."§r

§5"Craftadia won't 
end because of you 
my dear..."§r§r§r

§6"MissPortinari maybe?"§r 
§5“Wait... Did you just 
remember last ti-
      §c✮✯✮✯§r§r§r
#- §c✮✯§r
§dBefore §5ɨȶ§r §dcould finish, the air in the room shifted violently. 
A sharp burst of magic tore through the space. 
The shadow of§r §5ɨȶ§r §drecoiled, flickering wildly as a figure stepped through a shimmering portal that hadn’t been there a second ago.§r§r
#- §dLong silver hair gleamed in the dim light, emerald eyes locked on Sweetpea with intensity. 

§c"There you are Witch!"

§dBefore she could react, a hand shot out and grabbed her arm.

Sweetpea’s eyes widened. §6"Castien...
#- §"§6“What? What are you...”

§cCastien §dmuttered a sequence of numbers "§70010110§d", and the air around them seemed to collapse in on itself. 

The room began to twist and distort as Sweetpea felt the unmistakable pull of magic enveloping her.
#- §6“Wait, stop! What are you doing?!” §dshe shouted, struggling against his grip.

§5ɨȶ§r lunged forward, the §dentity surging like a storm cloud.§r §5“Release her!” §5§5§d§5ɨȶ§r §droared, his voice reverberating through the building.
But§r §cCastien §d§ didn’t even glance at the shadowy figure.
#- §dHis grip on Sweetpea tightened. And then, with a final surge of power, the two of them vanished, leaving the room empty and silent.

§5ɨȶ §dstood frozen, his form flickering. For the first time in eons, he felt something he hadn’t experienced in a long, long time: 
no control.
#- 



§dThe whisper that escaped §5ɨȶ's §dform was barely audible. 

§5“What… 
       just happened?”
