#-  §d╔═--═ஓ๑☠๑ஓ═--═╗§r
      Lantern's In 
     The Dark§rness
 §d╚═--═ஓ๑☠๑ஓ═--═╝§r §5Now... I've failed you! 
You are gone, and 
I can not find you.
I should've been faster, stronger, something more than what I am. I thought Soulcorp might 
give me answers. 
That hope is fading.§r
#- §5Their Lanterns, they were never meant to be touched. It's the only plan I could think of to save what was left of you my dear. 

I'm in what's left of §8Enocori's§r office. 
§5Ransacked, drawers torn open and papers scattered all over. 
They abandoned it 
in a hurry.§§
#- §5Soulcorp's resources are no longer spread across projects; they're all being funneled into one thing. 

     Summoning me.
             ☠
 They think I'm a God.

The documents I've pieced together paint a twisted picture.§r
#- §5Soulcorp believes I'm the key to surviving§r The Darkness§5. They're desperate to pull my physical form into this world, convinced I can deliver them from whatever end they see coming...

Looks like they had the same agenda all along my dear, just a little bit more insane.§r
#- §5They've sacrificed everything else for this, and worse, they've killed for it. The employee handbook said; anyone can call in their 'Uppers' for help, doing so will result in termination. You did not read the small print my dear... 
It's not a joke.
Termination is literal!§r
#- §5And then I found... him.

I thought §8Enocori§r 
§5was gone. He always seemed to know too much, like he was walking a tightrope. 

But he is not dead as everyone assumed. 

       Not exactly.
             ☠
      He is trapped.§r§r
#- §5A Lantern was placed on his desk. The only area that had less dust.

I could sense a soul inside, faint and flickering, trapped inside like a moth.

"Enocori?" 

I whispered, 
barely believing it.§r
#- §5His voice was faint, muffled by the magic, but I could hear the desperation in it. His whole life energy banging against the glass. I don't know how long he's been in there. Judging by the state of this place, it could've been weeks. Months. Maybe longer.
A prison with no key.
Nothing I could do.§r
#- §5He was your 'friend' not mine my dear!

Soulcorp sees me as their salvation, but they don't understand

       I'm no God... 
 ☠ɨ'ʍ ֆօ ʍʊƈɦ աօʀֆɛ☠

Sweetpea, wherever you are, I hope you're fighting. 
I hope you're safe.§r
#- §5I hope you're 
not giving up. 
       ...Because I have.

§8Enocori's§r banging §5grows weaker, his voice fading, I don't know how much longer he has, or anyone has. I don't care.

They wanted a God, §lWhat they'll get is a reckoning!§r§r
