#- §5╔═.✵.════════╗  §2     ᴛʜᴇ ᴘʀɪᴄᴇ ᴏꜰ          ꜰᴏʀᴇᴠᴇʀ ᴘᴀʀᴛ ᴏɴᴇ
§5╚════════.✵.═╝
§2Sweetpea hit the ground hard. 
The teleportation magic faded. She pushed herself up, eyes blazing as she turned on Castien. "§6What the hell was that...§2" she snapped. "§6Where am I?!§2"
#- §2Castien stood tall, his silver hair illuminated by the torchlight of the palace hall. His face was unreadable, ... his eyes cold.

"§cYou'll understand soon§2", he said, voice devoid of emotion. Sweetpea clenched her fists. "§6Oh, no, no. You do not get to...§2" The elf simply turned,
#- §2leading her down a long marble corridor. 

The walls were lined with grand banners bearing the crest of his house. An Emerald Crown, the mark for this royal family. 

For some reason it made her stomach twist, like she had seen it before. 
#- §2They entered a huge throne room. At the far end, seated on the throne, was §4King Theron§2. His gaze settled on her immediately, piercing. He was regal but unnerving. A cruel smirk on his face. Sweetpea did not blink and straightened, refusing to look intimidated.§r§r§r
#- §2"§6I'd love to know why I've been dragged here against my will?§2"

Theron chuckled, resting his chin against his fist. "§4Not many would speak to me so boldly... impressive.§2"

The king leaned forward slightly.
      "§4You're special...§2"
#- §2"§4You will make a fine addition to our family witch... powerful as you are.§2"

She felt the weight of his words. "§6You can't be serious§2", she muttered. For the first time, she turned to look at Castien. He remained silent, his fingers twitched slightly at his side.
#- §2"§4Take her,§2" Theron ordered. "§4She will be of great use to us soon enough.§2" Guards moved toward her, 
but Castien stepped forward. "§cI'll handle this,§2" he said. His voice was steady. Theron studied him for a moment, then waved his hand dismissively. Without a word Castien grabbed
#- §2Sweetpea's arm and pulled her from the throne room.

Only when they reached a secluded chamber did he finally release her. Sweetpea yanked her arm away, rage boiling over. She was about to attack him when... 

"§cI had no choice!§2"
#- §2Sweetpea crossed her arms. "§cTrust me, we'd both be dead§2". Castien put his head down in shame. Sweetpea narrowed her eyes. "§6Ohhh, this better 
be good!§2" 

Castien hesitated, 
then stepped closer, lowering his voice. "§0The Darkness §cis here, Sweetpea.§2"
#- §2"§cAnd I know how to survive it remember?§2"

Sweetpea frowned.
"§6What you told me in that cave, before we got interrupted...§2"

  §f§r§0 Immortality §f§r

§2"§cI know how to do it! How to break The Code! But I need to make sure it... works.§2" 
#- §2It took Sweetpea 
way to long for the 
words sink in.

"§6YOU WANT ME TO BE YOUR TEST SUBJECT!?§2"             she shouted.

"§cYou will be 'you' when the next world begins! You know deep down, this is your only option... your last hope! Take it!§2" 
#- §2She could recover everything she'd lost... "§6You don't know what it's like losing what you cannot be without.... fine, do it.§2"
Castien exhaled. "§cYes, I do.§2" He then took The Soultrap... Fern's sword, off the display case. "§cYou won't feel a thing,§2" he promised.
             
 🗡 She doubted that.
