My dear? 
Say something...
I need you!

I have to tell you 
the truth at least...

Who I am... or how much... I love you. §r😖
#- §5You're not coming back... are you?

... your silly potatoes.

Alright, I guess if 
I can't save you... 

I can 'use' you... 
and your magic too save...

Your readers!   
                       §6🥔§r§
#- §6╔═◦🥔§◦════════╗§r
      §5The Emotional           Support Potato
        §dᴘᴀʀᴛ ᴏɴᴇ§r    
§6╚════════◦🥔§◦═╝
§5For so long, ɨȶ had believed the answer was in the lanterns. 

Convinced himself 
and the witch he loved that they were the key to stopping 
§0The Darkness.
#- §5But the more he uncovered, the clearer it became. 
The lanterns preserved agony, feeding off suffering, hoarding souls like currency.

And in the end, they would do nothing. Maybe for Soulcorp... but not the people he cared about.
#- §5But she could.

§6Sweetpea.

§5She had been planning something all along. Something absurd.  Something so... ridiculous and human of her that he had not even considered 
it as real magic.

Potatoes!
#- §5Not just any potatoes; Emotional Support Potatoes!

He could still hear her laughing about them, insisting that everyone needs an ESP. She had made hundreds, stuffing them into people's hands, into their homes, into their pockets. 
#- §5It had been a 
joke at first. 
Soft, enchanted potatoes, each carefully marked, carefully shared, infused with warmth and an energy that, 
at the time, had seemed so small.

But now, standing in her abandoned tavern, ɨȶ understood.
#- 
§k§70010110§k001011000101100010110001011000101100010110§l§00010110§7§k00101100010110001011§00010110§k00101100010110001011000101100010110§70010110§k00101100010110001011000101100010110001011000101100010110§00010110§k0010110001001100010110001011100111011001
