§5╚════════.✵.═╝
§2The moon hung heavy in the sky, its pale light spilling over the ruins of the once magnificent elven temple. Sweetpea stood in the middle of the circle, her heart pounding. Across from her, Castien gripped
#- §2the hilt of The Soultrap. Humming with an unnatural energy.

"§6Why do you have it?§2" she whispered. She didn't have to ask. 

She already knew.

He didn't speak at first, only exhaled slowly. "§cBecause 
Fern is gone.§2"
#- §2Sweetpea felt her stomach drop. Fern the warrior, the unstoppable force, the woman Castien loved more than life itself. Gone!

She wanted to say something, but words would not fill the chasm of his grief. 
He must have lost her since the last time 
#- §2they all met... in that strange snowy battle.

And somehow, he had survived. Somehow, he had kept going. 

Now the King's demands made much more sense. He wanted a new wife for his son.

And now, Castien was doing this for her.
#- §2The ritual had to work. If it didn't, §0Darkness §2would come like it always did, swallowing everything whole, erasing lives, rewriting fates.

Castien pointed the Soultrap towards her. It glowed with eerie light, reacting to the spell he wove around them both.
#- §2His hands trembled, his voice steady but thick with emotion as he chanted the incantation. Sweetpea felt the energy coil around her, seep into her skin, pulling at 
the very core 
of her soul. 

It was working!
But something 
was wrong...
#- §2A searing pain burned through her chest. 

She gasped, stumbling back. The ritual demanded more than just magic. 

It demanded sacrifice.

"§cSweetpea!§2" Castien's voice cracked, eyes wide with horror. 
        It was too late...
#- §2The magic surged, 
wild and unstoppable, pulling her straight into the blade!

A storm of memories exploded in her mind. Past lives flashing before her in brilliant, painful clarity. 
Faces she had long forgotten. People she had loved. People she had lost. Everything!
#- §2And then, the truth.

She knew she would never get home. That this was always going to be a one way ticket.
§5ɨȶ§r would be all alone.

§2This was the price. She had saved herself from§r §0The Darkness§2, but at the cost of this version of herself.
#- §2The pain faded. Replaced by a weightless...
quiet peace.

Castien was crying.

She tried to smile, though her body was already dying.

"§6I forgive you.§2" were her last words. The last thing she saw...
#- §2was his face, twisted in grief, the Soultrap still clutched in his shaking hands.

For her final seconds she pictured what her next life could be like... and if §5ɨȶ§r would §2be there. He always was!

And then...§r
§0Everything went black.
#- ████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████
