§6╚════════◦🥔§◦═╝
§5The lanterns had been built to isolate, to trap, to keep people afraid. 

But Sweetpea's potatoes? 
They had been 
built to connect.
#- §5Every single ESP carried a piece of whoever was blessed to own one. Hope, kindness, laughter. 
The magic inside 
them wasn't about suffering; it was 
about community! 
About shared strength. About defying §0The Darkness §5together instead of standing alone.
#- §5And she had hidden 
the answer in plain sight.

A slow, stunned smile spread across ɨȶ's face. "Of course. Of course you would do this, you brilliant, sneaky witch...".

The Emotional Support Potatoes were a network, a backup
#- §5woven through the very people of Craftadia! 

§0The Darkness §5sought to erase everything, to reset memories and souls like they had never existed. 

But as long as people had an ESP. By 
chance or because they earned it...
#- §5as long as even one of them remained... 

Their stories 
would endure!

Sweetpea had given them a chance to survive. 

A way to fight back!

And ɨȶ would make sure this worked.
#- §5He knelt down, placing Sweetpea's special personal potato on the wooden floor. 
It was warm in his hands, pulsing with magic, not just hers, but the magic of every soul who 
had one.

Slowly, carefully, 
ɨȶ began to 
weave a spell.
#- §5The potato shimmered, absorbing the collective energy, linking each person together in ways Soulcorp could never comprehend. 

This was the power he had been searching for. Not pain. Not isolation. But love. 
And Sweetpea had known all along.
#- §5He let out a breath.
He didn't know what would happen next, if he would see her again, if she would even remember him when this was all over, if this spell had even worked. But he knew one thing.

If anyone could survive §0The Darkness... §5it was her.
#- 


§5And how her silly... 

ridiculous...

enchanted potato... 

brought an entire 
community together!§r
